      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3725_Start3" name="Reporter/witness/investigator involved in a case; retaliation report">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3725_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3725_Task4" name="Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer/HR monitor reporters/witnesses/investigators for…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer/HR monitor reporters/witnesses/investigators for retaliation: track adverse actions (discipline, schedule/perf-change, transfer, exclusion) post-report for a defined period, and investigate any pattern suggestive of retaliation
Responsible (R): Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer / HR
Accountable (A): Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3725_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3725_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3725_Task5" name="Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer/HR/Legal investigate any retaliation allegation…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer/HR/Legal investigate any retaliation allegation: substantiate, take corrective action against the retaliator (links to W3724), restore/protect the reporter, and document; treat retaliation as serious misconduct itself
Responsible (R): Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer / HR / Legal
Accountable (A): Ethics Committee
Duration: On allegation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3725_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3725_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3725_Task6" name="Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer report retaliation incidents and protection posture…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer report retaliation incidents and protection posture to the Ethics Committee (W3719) and board audit committee (links to VS-36); reinforce anti-retaliation culture (links to W3718)
Responsible (R): Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer
Accountable (A): Ethics Committee
Duration: Quarterly + on incident</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3725_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3725_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3725_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3725_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
